  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"terminal#9218\", \"terminal#3454\", \"terminal#18937\"], \"answer\": \"Both parts of this request have been reported before. The width request is tracked in terminal#9218 (verticalScrollBarWidth). Related width requests, terminal#12395, terminal#15113 and terminal#18937, were closed as duplicates or declined. The team said it doesn't want to add per-app scrollbar sizing and would rather see this handled system-wide, so a Terminal-only width setting is unlikely. Until the platform changes, you can do two things. (1) The always-visible request was tracked in terminal#3454 and shipped as the \\\"Always\\\" scrollbar visibility option in Terminal 1.17. Set it under Settings > [Profile or Defaults] > Appearance > Scrollbar visibility: Always. Terminal also follows the Windows setting that turns off \\\"Automatically hide scroll bars\\\", under Settings > Accessibility > Visual effects. (2) For width, add your accessibility need to terminal#9218. You could also raise it with the WinUI team (microsoft-ui-xaml#6684) or through Windows Feedback, because the scrollbar comes from WinUI.\"}",
